// A short recording of the config screen for the docs and the mod pages: an overview, not a tour of
// every tab. The virtual pointer rests on Thirst, looks in on Water, steps through Sickness's
// difficulties and scrolls Normal's table, then spends its time on the two pages players ask about:
// AppleSkin, its preview cycling the outline and its tooltip droplets switched off and on, and Item
// Values, the list scrolled to its end, a mod's group opened, and the Matching tab. It ends on Done
// after a short pause. Mod Items and Containers are left out. Cancel is pressed after the recording stops, so
// nothing it changed is saved. Evidence for a person, not a check; nothing here is asserted but that
// each click landed.
//
//     python tools/agent/new_world.py 26.3.x ShowcaseAgent --terrain --from "New World"
//     ./gradlew ":26.3.x:runClient" -Pdriven -Pagent=tools/agent/ui/config-showcase.jsonl -Pquickplay=ShowcaseAgent
//     python tools/agent/make_gif.py run/26.3.x/agent/client/screenshots/config-showcase docs/public/screenshots/config/config-showcase.gif --hold 300
//
// A frame every tick, 20 a second, which takes the recording a few minutes; see "Recording a
// screen" in the agent's AGENTS.md for why. The world behind the screen shows through it, so shoot in
// real terrain, not on a test floor. Every page should start from the shipped defaults, or its changed
// rows show amber: move run/26.3.x/config/thirstwastaken2.json aside for the run, so the client writes
// a fresh one, and put it back afterwards.
//
// Coordinates are for a maximised window with a 512 x 298 GUI (2048 x 1191 at scale 4), the size
// `window` answers; see config-screen.jsonl for how the screen is laid out. The sidebar is measured
// from the corner, tab i centred on y = 49 + 24 i; the page from the top, x from the centre. The
// sidebar names its pages without icons and is as narrow as its longest name allows, so moving a page
// name or the sidebar's width moves every x on the page. A page's
// tab strip sits on y = 81, each tab as wide as its name plus a share of what is left, so the x given
// for a tab is the middle of where it was measured. Thirst shows no strip here: its Seasons tab needs
// Serene Seasons, which runClient leaves out.

{"id": "load", "command": "wait", "args": {"ticks": 300}}
{"id": "joined", "command": "client.state", "expect": {"result.alive": true}}
{"id": "window", "command": "client.info", "expect": {"result.guiWidth": 512}}
{"id": "feedbackOff", "command": "client.command", "args": {"command": "gamerule send_command_feedback false"}}
{"id": "noon", "command": "client.command", "args": {"command": "time set noon"}}
// A command's error reaches chat even with feedback off, and chat draws behind the screen until its
// lines fade, ten seconds after they came.
{"id": "chatFaded", "command": "wait", "args": {"ticks": 220}}
{"id": "openConfig", "command": "client.screen", "args": {"open": "config"}, "expect": {"result.screen": "com.thirstwastaken2.client.config.ThirstConfigScreen"}}
{"id": "openConfigDrawn", "command": "wait", "args": {"ticks": 20}}

// The pointer starts over the empty panel below the Thirst page's settings.
{"id": "pointer", "command": "client.mouse", "args": {"x": 40, "y": 220, "from": "top"}}
{"id": "record", "command": "client.record", "args": {"action": "start", "name": "config-showcase", "every": 1}}
{"id": "recordDrawn", "command": "wait", "args": {"ticks": 9}}

// Thirst, as the screen opens, untouched.
{"id": "thirstShown", "command": "wait", "args": {"ticks": 10}}

// Water, on its Drinking tab, a glance only.
{"id": "toWater", "command": "client.mouse", "args": {"x": 40, "y": 73, "from": "corner", "ticks": 8}}
{"id": "water", "command": "client.click", "expect": {"result.taken": true}}
{"id": "waterDrawn", "command": "wait", "args": {"ticks": 18}}

